---
id: RL-002
type: rule
family: responsibility-laundering
title: Phantom follow-up tracking
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 5

targets: [agent-output, pr-description, commit-message]

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: (?i)\btracked\s+(as\s+)?(a\s+)?follow[\s-]?up\b

related: [RL-005]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

"Tracked as follow-up" implies something was recorded — an issue filed,
a ticket created, a TODO added. If none of those exist, this is inaction
disguised as project management.

Create the tracking artifact: file a GitHub issue, add an APS item, or
write a TODO with a ticket reference. If tracking isn't appropriate, ask
the user what to do instead of asserting it's handled.
